{"id":"word:hebrew:H2691","type":"word","title":"חָצֵר","subtitle":"H2691 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a yard (as inclosed by a fence); also a hamlet (as similarly surrounded with walls)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to חָצֵר (H2691) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 190 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"חָצֵר (châtsêr) means a yard (as inclosed by a fence); also a hamlet (as similarly surrounded with walls) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 4 32."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"חָצֵר","transliteration":"châtsêr","pronunciation":"khaw-tsare'","strong":"H2691","lemmaId":"hebrew:H2691","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["וְ/חַצְרֵי/הֶֽן","הֶ/חָצֵ֥ר","הֶֽ/חָצֵר֙","הֶ/חָצֵ֖ר","הֶ/חָצֵֽר"],"morphs":[["HTd/Ncbsa",65],["HC/Ncbpc/Sp3fp",26],["HR/Ncbsc",20],["HRd/Ncbsa",15],["HR/Ncbpc",9],["HTd/Ncbpa",7],["HNcbsa",6],["HNcbsc",5],["HNcbpc",4],["HNcbpa",4]]},"definitions":{"short":"a yard (as inclosed by a fence); also a hamlet (as similarly surrounded with walls)","usage":"court, tower, village.","full":"H2691. chatser I. חָצֵר 145 noun masculine Ezek 40:23 and (oftener) feminine 1Kin 6:36 enclosure, court — absolute ׳ח 7:8 +, חָצֵרָה Jer 36:20 ; construct חֲצַר Exod 27:9 +; suffix חֲצֵרוֺ 2Sam 17:18 ; חֲצֵרוֺת Exod 8:9 4 t.; construct חַצְרֵי Neh 13:7 , הַצְרוֺת 2Kin 21:5 10 t.; suffix חֲצֵרָ֑י Isa 1:12 ; Zech 3:7 ; חֲצֵרֶיךָ Psa 65:5 ; 84:11 ; חֲצֵרוֺתָ֑י 1Chr 28:6 ; חֲצֵרֹתָיו Psa 100:4 , לְחַצְרוֺתָ֑יו 96:8 , וּבְחַצְרֹתֵיהֶם Neh 8:16 ; &#8212; 1 enclosures (in Egypt),perhaps court-yards, or cattle-yards, distinct from houses and from fields Exod 8:9 (J). 2 court of private house 2Sam 17:18 (containing well), compare Neh 8:16 ; of a palace, הָאַחֶרֶת חָצֵר 1Kin 7:8 the other court , immediately surrounding palace, so called in distinct. from ׳(הֶ)ח הַגְּדוֺלָה 7:9 ; 7:12 the great court , including ׳ח ׳הא and ׳הֶח הַמְּנִימִית of temple (see 3b ) in one great enclosure (see Sta Salomos Bauten, ZAW 1883. 152 f. ); 2Kin 20:4 (Qr Vrss The Kmp Klo and others; Kt Ke and others הָעִיר ), Jer 36:20 ; Est 1:5 ; 2:11 ; 4:11 ; 5:1-2 , 6:4 (twice in verse); 6:5 ; ׳ח מַטָּרָה court of guard , place of (honourable) confinement Jer 32:2 (in king's house), 32:8 ; 32:12 ; 33:1 ; 37:21 (twice in verse); 38:6 , 13 , 28 ; 39:14-15 ,. Especially 3. a. court of tabernacle הַמִּשְׁכָּן חֲצַר Exod 27:9 , compare 27:9 ; 27:12 ; 27:13 24t. Exodus (all P; הֶח ׳שַׁעַר gate of the court 35:17 ; 38:15 , 18 , 31 ; 39:40 ; 40:8 , 33 ); Lev 6:9 ; 6:19 ; Num 3:26 (twice in verse) ( ׳הֶח מֶּתַח ), 3:37 ; 4:26 (twice in verse) ( הֶח שַׁעַר ׳מֶּתַח ), 4:32 ; courts of house of ׳י 1Chr 23:28 . b. court(s) of Solomon's temple, inner with ׳הֶח הַמְּנִימִית 1Kin 6:36 ; 7:12 (but on text see Sta l. c .) Ezek 8:16 ; 10:3 compare 10:4 ; = upper with ׳הֶח הָעֶלְיוֺן Jer 36:10 (see Gf), and ׳ח הַכֹּהֲנִים 2Chr 4:9 (where also הַגְּדוֺלָה הָעֲזָרָה , as often Ezek., also לָעֲזָרָה דְּלָתוֺת ); outer court הַחִיצֹנָה ׳הֶח Ezek 10:5 = ׳הֶח הַחֲדָשָׁה 2Chr 20:5 ; see further 1Kin 8:64 2Chr 7:7 ; 24:21 ; 29:16 ; Jer 19:14 ; 26:2 ; Ezek 8:7 ; two courts 2Kin 21:5 2Chr 33:5 ; 2Kin 23:12 ; courts Ezek 9:7 ; 1Chr 28:12 ; 2Chr 23:5 ; Neh 8:1 , 6 ; 13:7 ; often in poetry, courts of ׳י Isa 1:12 ; 62:9 ( ׳ח קדשׁי ), Zech 3:7 ; Psa 65:5 ; 84:3 ; 84:11 ; 96:8 ; 100:4 ; 116:19 ; 135:2 c. courts of Ezekiel's temple Ezek 40:14 38 t. Ezekiel 40-46 (of these read הַשַּׁעַר for החצר 40:19 , 32 with ᵐ5 Hi Co; and החיצון for החצר 41:15 with ᵐ5 Ew Co). ** 42:6 הַחִיצֹנוֺת for הַחֲצֵרוֺת . II. חצר (√ of following; compare Arabic be present, settle or dwell , see Lag BN 47 f. ; Sabean חצֿר fixed abode Os (Levy) ZMG 1865, 185 CIS iv, 1. 2, No. 79. 82 ). II. [ חָצֵר ] 46 noun masculine Neh 11:25 settled abode, settlement, village (Lag l. c .) — always plural, absolute חֲצֵרִים Josh 19:8 5 t.; construct חַצְרֵי 1Chr 9:16 ; Neh 12:28 ; suffix חֲצֵרֶיהָ Josh 21:12 4 t.; חַצְרֵיהֶם 1Chr 4:33 6 t.; חַצְרֵיהֶן Josh 13:23-24 t. Joshua; &#8212; a. settlements of Ishmaelites Gen 25:16 (P; || טִירוֺת circles of tents); of עַוִּים Deut 2:23 ; of Kedar Isa 42:11 (|| עָרִים ); סָבִיב חֹמָה אֵיןלָֿהֶם אֲשֶׁר הַחֲצֵרִים בָּתֵּי Lev 25:31 (H), houses of the villages which have no wall about them ; חֲצֵרִים מַאֲרַב Psa 10:8 lurking-place(s) of villages (i.e. where oppressor, as a wild beast, watches his opportunity to attack the defenceless). Usu. b. as dependencies of cities Josh 15:46 , with בְּנֹתֶיהָ (see above בַּת 4 p. 123) Josh 15:45 , 47 (twice in verse) (all J E ?); ׳וְכָלהַֿח הֶעָרִים סְבִיבוֺת אֲשֶׁר 19:8 (P), also 21:12 (P), = 1Chr 6:41 ; Neh 12:29 ; also Josh 13:23 , 28 ; 15:32 23 t. Joshua (all P), Neh 11:25 , 30 (|| בָּנוֺת 11:25 ; 11:27 etc.), 12:28 . c. villages, not contrasted with cities (compare Isa 42:11 above) 1Chr 9:16 , 22 , 25 (all of Levites). d. ׳ח apparently including all settlements outside of Jerusalem בִּשְׂדֹתָם ׳הַח Neh 11:25 . &#8212; ׳ח in proper name, of a location see below (and see Bla on Josh 15:20-32 ).","rootNote":"(masculine and feminine); from 2690 in its original sense;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 4 32","keyReferences":["1Chr 4 32","1Chr 4 33","1Chr 6 41","1Chr 9 16","1Chr 9 22","1Chr 9 25","1Chr 23 28","1Chr 28 6"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":190,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 4 32","book":"1Chr","chapter":4,"verse":32,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/חַצְרֵי/הֶם֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncbpc/Sp3mp"},{"reference":"1Chr 4 33","book":"1Chr","chapter":4,"verse":33,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חַצְרֵי/הֶ֗ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcbpc/Sp3mp"},{"reference":"1Chr 6 41","book":"1Chr","chapter":6,"verse":41,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חֲצֵרֶ֑י/הָ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcbpc/Sp3fs"},{"reference":"1Chr 9 16","book":"1Chr","chapter":9,"ve